简直暴力得惨绝人寰。
It is a mother of violence.

414
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,200
马力也相当够看。
The power's not bad either.

415
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:18,567
零到六十英里加速
只要六秒半，
0-60 takes
six-and-half seconds

416
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:22,233
油门踩到底
极速能飙到150英里。
and flat out
you'd be going at 150.

417
00:21:26,267 --> 00:21:28,267
克拉克森：说到这儿，
你们肯定有人会想：
CLARKSON: At this point,
some of you
are going to think,

418
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:34,167
“天呐，那它岂不是没有
新款沃克斯豪尔雅特VXR快？”
"Oh, dear, that means
it's not as fast as
the new Vauxhall Astra VXR."

419
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:38,167
确实如此，
但那台沃克斯豪尔马力过大了。
That's true enough,
but the Vauxhall has
too much power.

420
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:41,500
扭矩转向剧烈得
跟一头乱拱的蠢猪一样。
It torque steers
like an absolute pig.

421
00:21:41,533 --> 00:21:44,700
而且它比这台车
还贵了整整1500镑。
And it's £1,500
more expensive than this.

422
00:21:44,733 --> 00:21:49,900
所以要是白送我一台沃克斯豪尔，
我肯定爱不释手，绝对力挺到底。
So if given a Vauxhall,
I'd love it, I really would,
and I'd defend it to the hilt.

423
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:52,067
但我会自掏腰包
去买一台吗？
But would I buy one
with money?

424
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,400
绝不。
No.

425
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:56,400
这台“ASBO”要好得多。
The ASBO is a much better car.

426
00:21:56,433 --> 00:22:01,367
它舒服得多，
而且当你想要找乐子的时候，
它也完全听话好开。
It's much more comfortable,
and it's manageable
when you wanna have fun.

427
00:22:01,933 --> 00:22:03,800
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

428
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:10,200
前轮有着极其强大的抓地力，
There is immense grip
from the front end

429
00:22:10,233 --> 00:22:14,033
而且因为采用了
跟老款福克斯相同的
and because it has
the same control blade
rear suspension

430
00:22:14,067 --> 00:22:15,733
“刀锋式”后悬挂，
as you have in the old Focus,

431
00:22:15,767 --> 00:22:19,067
你在收油时还能获得超多
妙不可言的甩尾乐趣。
you get loads of lovely
lift-off over steer as well.

432
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:20,767
（大笑）哎呦喂！
(LAUGHING) Wey!

433
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:25,133
再甩一下！
And flick!

434
00:22:25,167 --> 00:22:26,600
嘿-嘿！
Hey-hey!

435
00:22:30,533 --> 00:22:32,033
这车操控简直神了。
It's a brilliant handling car.

436
00:22:32,067 --> 00:22:35,233
我是说，
真的太绝了。
I mean,
it's absolutely brilliant.

437
00:22:35,267 --> 00:22:38,500
噢！就算你能把车开出埃塞克斯……
Oh! You can take
the car out of Essex...

438
00:22:38,533 --> 00:22:39,600
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLING)

439
00:22:44,267 --> 00:22:46,367
而且坐在里面也很惬意，
It's a nice place
to sit, as well,

440
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:51,433
尤其是考虑到，我此刻其实是坐在
So Solid Crew乐团的某只大球鞋里面。
especially when you bear in
mind that I am actually inside
one of So Solid Crew's shoes.

441
00:22:51,467 --> 00:22:54,100
这座椅简直棒极了。
The seats are especially fab.

442
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:56,267
既舒服，包裹支撑又到位。
Comfortable and supportive.

443
00:23:00,367 --> 00:23:02,800
克拉克森：它甚至都算不上
是个狂饮暴食的“酒鬼”。
CLARKSON: It's not even
what you'd call
a binge drinker.

444
00:23:02,833 --> 00:23:05,567
养起来就跟买的时候一样便宜。
It'll be as cheap to run
as it is to buy.

445
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:08,233
这台只要17500英镑。
This model's only £17,500.

446
00:23:10,067 --> 00:23:11,400
可靠性怎么样？
Reliability?

447
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:14,100
这么说吧，我自己家里
就有一台Y牌照的老福克斯，
Well, all I can say is
I have a Y reg Focus at home

448
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:15,800
它从来没出过哪怕一次毛病。
and it has never
gone wrong once.

449
00:23:15,833 --> 00:23:18,567
是我拥有过最省心的车了。
Most dependable car
I've ever owned.

450
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:20,367
但这台新车呢，
稍微复杂了点。
This one is
a bit more complicated.

451
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:24,733
它配了可调转向，
能调成沉重、
轻盈或者标准模式。
It's got adjustable steering
to make it heavy
or light or normal.

452
00:23:27,467 --> 00:23:29,867
说实话，这纯粹就是
多了一个坏掉的由头。
To be honest, that's just
something to go wrong.

453
00:23:31,033 --> 00:23:32,367
但至少
人在里面应该挺安全的。
But at least
he should be safe.

454
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:34,667
这台“暴徒车”拿到了NCAP
五星安全碰撞评级，
The ASBO has an NCAP
five star rating

455
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:37,100
对行人的保护也相当好。
and is good for
pedestrians, as well.

456
00:23:37,133 --> 00:23:39,233
我是说，行人总不可能
直接走到大马路上说：
I mean, it's not like
we gonna step into
the road and say,

457
00:23:39,267 --> 00:23:40,867
“我根本没看见它冲过来！”
"I never saw it coming!"

458
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:42,467
（引擎轰鸣）
(ROARING)

459
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:45,400
所以它还真称得上是面面俱到。
So it really does seem to have
all the bases covered.

460
00:23:45,433 --> 00:23:49,233
价格便宜、安全、
舒适、实用，
It's cheap, it's safe,
it's comfortable,
it's practical,

461
00:23:49,267 --> 00:23:52,367
开起来更是无与伦比。
and it is truly amazing
to drive.

462
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:54,967
而最棒的一点呢？
And the best thing?

463
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:57,367
它其实还有蓝色可选。
It's also available in blue.

464
00:24:00,967 --> 00:24:02,567
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

465
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:09,100
尽管赛道当时已经完全湿透了，
Even though,
the track was soaking wet,

466
00:24:09,133 --> 00:24:13,100
但这玩意儿抓地力强到
过弯时后轮都能翘起来。
this thing has so much grip
it was kicking up a back wheel
in the corners.

467
00:24:13,133 --> 00:24:15,067
-确实太神了。
-不可思议，完全赞同。
-That is amazing.
-That is incredible, agreed.

468
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:19,600
但福特之前不是说
要出一款RS版的福克斯吗，
But didn't Ford say
they were going to make
an RS version of the Focus

469
00:24:19,633 --> 00:24:21,233
说是还要更加……
with like even more...

470
00:24:21,267 --> 00:24:22,633
噢，对，没跑，他们说过。
Oh, yeah, no, they did.

471
00:24:22,667 --> 00:24:24,133
他们说过会有300匹制动马力，
They said it was going to have
300 horse brake power,

472
00:24:24,167 --> 00:24:25,367
还会有四轮驱动，
it was going to be
four wheel drive,

473
00:24:25,367 --> 00:24:27,700
车侧还贴着阿迪达斯条纹，没错！
Adidas stripes
down the side, yeah!

474
00:24:27,733 --> 00:24:30,167
-那车后来怎么样了？
-他们懒得折腾了。
-So what happened to that?
-They couldn't be bothered.

475
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,367
他们真正搞出来的是那个。
What they're actually
doing is that.

476
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,900
噢，是的。这就是Iosis。
Oh, yes. This is the Iosis.

477
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:38,833
它是福特的一款概念车，
我知道它看着有点像轿跑，
It's a Ford concept car
and I know it looks
a bit like a Coupe

478
00:24:38,867 --> 00:24:43,733
但它骨子里其实是一台
四门四座的家用轿车。
but it is in fact,
a four seat, four door
family saloon.

479
00:24:43,767 --> 00:24:48,933
最关键的一点在于，
这台车，本质上就是下一代福特蒙迪欧。
And the important thing
is that this, in essence,
is the new Ford Mondeo.

480
00:24:48,967 --> 00:24:53,367
哇！所以蒙迪欧
竟然要配鸥翼门了？
Wow! So the Mondeo
is going to have
gull-wing doors?

481
00:24:53,367 --> 00:24:55,367
只不过它不会配鸥翼门。
Except it won't have
gull-wing doors.

482
00:24:55,367 --> 00:24:57,400
也没了潜水料座椅！
And neoprene seats!

483
00:24:57,433 --> 00:24:59,833
其实他们根本不打算用潜水料座椅。
Actually they're not
doing the neoprene seats.

484
00:24:59,867 --> 00:25:02,833
那会用摄像头取代后视镜吗？
Is it going to have cameras
instead of wing mirrors?

485
00:25:02,867 --> 00:25:06,667
很遗憾，他们也不会
用摄像头代替后视镜。
Sadly, they're not
going to do cameras
instead of wing mirrors.

486
00:25:06,700 --> 00:25:08,367
那它能在天花板上开吗？
Will it be able to drive
on the ceiling

487
00:25:08,367 --> 00:25:11,567
就像刚才短片里
那辆福克斯ST一样？
like the ST Focus did
in that film we just saw?

488
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:12,967
-不能。
-行吧。
-No.
-Right.

489
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:15,567
别管那些花里胡哨的小玩意和噱头了。
Forget all the gadgetry
stuff and all the flim-flam.

490
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:19,467
重点是，
下一代蒙迪欧差不多就长这样。
The important thing is
this is the next Mondeo
will look like.

491
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:21,233
我觉得帅呆了。
I think it looks fantastic.

492
00:25:21,267 --> 00:25:23,467
确实帅，看着像辆阿斯顿·马丁。
It does. It looks like
an Aston Martin.

493
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:25,567
不过话说回来，
概念归概念，回到当下，
Thing is though,
that's then and this is now

494
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,700
该把我们车队的御用赛车手，
and it's time to put
our team racing driver

495
00:25:29,233 --> 00:25:31,100
塞进那辆福克斯ST里了。
in the Focus ST.

496
00:25:31,133 --> 00:25:34,467
有人说，他的政治立场极度吓人；
Some say that his politics
are terrifying,

497
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:38,233
还有人说，他曾一拳撂倒过一匹马。
and that he once punched
a horse to the ground.

498
00:25:38,267 --> 00:25:40,433
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

499
00:25:40,467 --> 00:25:44,267
我们只知道，
他叫斯提格！
All we know is that
he's called The Stig.

500
00:25:44,367 --> 00:25:46,000
克拉克森：今天外头大雾弥漫，
CLARKSON: It's very foggy
out there today,

501
00:25:46,033 --> 00:25:48,633
但你会注意到斯提格没开后雾灯，
but you'll notice
The Stig doesn't have
his rear fog lights on,

502
00:25:48,667 --> 00:25:51,367
因为显而易见，他又不是个彻头彻尾的蠢蛋。
'cause, of course he's not
a blithering idiot.

503
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:54,267
噢，他又放起了他的巴洛克古典乐。
Oh, here he is with
his Baroque Classics.

504
00:25:54,367 --> 00:25:56,233
天哪，怎么还不见车影？
Oh, heavens,
why is he not coming up?

505
00:25:56,267 --> 00:25:58,367
-（轮胎尖叫声）
-他过来了吗？
-(TYRES SQUEALING)
-Is he coming up?

506
00:25:58,367 --> 00:26:01,733
等等，又是一声轮胎嘶鸣，
我猜他是在过一号弯。
Hang on, another tyre
squeal round, what I think
is the first corner there.

507
00:26:01,767 --> 00:26:03,800
没错，那是芝加哥弯，我认得那声音。
Right, that's Chicago.
I recognise that.

508
00:26:03,833 --> 00:26:05,367
他冲过来了！
He's coming through.

509
00:26:05,367 --> 00:26:06,567
斯提格开车当然用不着看路。
Stig, of course doesn't need
to see where he's going.

510
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,367
与其说是人，他更像台机器。
He's more machine than man.

511
00:26:08,367 --> 00:26:10,700
他眼里的世界全由数字构成。
噢等等，并没有！
He just sees in numbers.
Oh, no, wait, he doesn't!

512
00:26:10,733 --> 00:26:12,500
瞧，他刚才还是得看路的。
There, he did need to see
where he was going.

513
00:26:12,533 --> 00:26:14,433
现在他正杀向锤头弯。
Now he's down off
to the Hammer Head.

514
00:26:14,467 --> 00:26:16,267
他会记得刹车吗？
踩了！
Will he remember to brake?
Yes, he has.

515
00:26:16,367 --> 00:26:17,733
-干得漂亮，斯提格。
-（轮胎尖叫声）
-Well done, Stig.
-(TYRES SQUEALING)

516
00:26:17,767 --> 00:26:21,100
不得不说，大雾天里的赛道
可真够滑的。
Quite greasy out there,
must be said in the fog.

517
00:26:21,133 --> 00:26:23,900
不过漂得漂亮。
好样的，小斯提格！
Nice though.
Well done, Stiggy!

518
00:26:23,933 --> 00:26:26,733
现在正全速冲向 Follow Through 弯。
Now belting up
to the follow through.

519
00:26:26,767 --> 00:26:29,100
人跑哪儿去了？
来，听听声音。
Where's he gone?
Now, let's listen.

520
00:26:29,133 --> 00:26:31,900
听上去他刚才根本没收油。
不过也说不大准。
It didn't sound like
he lifted there.
Hard to say for sure.

521
00:26:31,933 --> 00:26:35,200
冲过来了，
穿过轮胎墙，
看着真快。
Coming up now,
through the tyre wall,
that looks quick.

522
00:26:35,233 --> 00:26:37,433
今天的斯提格胆子真肥。
He's a very brave Stig today.

523
00:26:37,467 --> 00:26:40,767
切入进弯，我猜
这是倒数第二个弯。
Turning in to what I think
is the second-last corner.

524
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:43,200
正在逼近甘邦弯。
And coming up to Gambon.

525
00:26:43,233 --> 00:26:44,900
进弯时
有一点转向过度。
Bit of over steer
going in there.

526
00:26:44,933 --> 00:26:46,900
冲线！
And across the line.

527
00:26:46,933 --> 00:26:49,100
虽然我完全不知道
他走的是哪条走线，
I've no idea
which line that was,

528
00:26:49,133 --> 00:26:53,533
但我手上拿到成绩了，
1分34秒9。
but I've got the time here,
one minute 34.9.

529
00:26:53,567 --> 00:26:55,400
呃，大家得记住，
Er, now you've got
to remember,

530
00:26:55,433 --> 00:26:58,000
这成绩在榜上排得挺靠后的，
但问题是，
当时的赛道又湿又滑。
that's quite a long way down,
but the thing is,
that was a greasy track.

531
00:26:58,033 --> 00:26:59,767
要是在大干地上，
我敢打包票，
On a dry track,
I am absolutely certain

532
00:26:59,800 --> 00:27:03,800
它绝对能跑赢
雅特VXR
和高尔夫GTI。
this would be quicker
than an Astra VXR
and a Golf GTI.

533
00:27:03,833 --> 00:27:05,200
这车确实棒极了。
It's a very good car.

534
00:27:05,233 --> 00:27:06,833
好，现在得进入下一环节了，
Right, now we got to move on,

535
00:27:06,867 --> 00:27:09,267
因为今晚
我们要打破一下常规。
because we're having
a bit of a break
from the norm tonight.

536
00:27:09,367 --> 00:27:12,400
因为我们要把一位国会议员，
Because we're going to put
a member of Parliament

537
00:27:12,433 --> 00:27:14,467
塞进咱们的廉价车里。
in our reasonably-priced car.

538
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:15,800
他是交通事务大臣，
He is the
Minister for Transport,

539
00:27:15,833 --> 00:27:18,733
这也就意味着，他就是
“测速摄像头大臣”。
which means he is the minister
for speed cameras.

540
00:27:18,767 --> 00:27:20,167
观众：（狂嘘）嘘——！
AUDIENCE: Boo!

541
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:21,967
噢，别这样，别这样。
Oh, no, no.

542
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:26,367
这里可是BBC。
我们会以充满敬意且客观公正的态度
对待他。
This is the BBC.
We will treat him with
respect and impartiality.

543
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:30,933
所以掌声欢迎，
魔王本尊——
斯蒂芬·莱迪曼博士！
So please welcome,
Beelzebub himself,
Dr Stephen Ladyman!

544
00:27:30,967 --> 00:27:32,567
（全场欢呼）
(ALL CHEERING)

545
00:27:34,033 --> 00:27:35,433
你好啊！
How are you?

546
00:27:35,467 --> 00:27:38,200
-（部分观众狂嘘）
-不行，咱们可不兴这样！
-(SECTIONS OF AUDIENCE BOO)
-No, we won't have that!

547
00:27:41,633 --> 00:27:43,900
至少目前还没人
把蛋挞派扣在你脸上，
At least no one
shoved the custard pie
in your face yet,

548
00:27:43,933 --> 00:27:45,433
那可是我切切实实挨过的待遇。
which is what really
happens to me.

549
00:27:45,467 --> 00:27:47,367
不得不说，
你可真是个勇士。
You are a brave soul,
I have to say.

550
00:27:47,367 --> 00:27:50,433
台下可都是Top Gear的观众。
你自己吃过多少张超速罚单？
You are Top Gear audience.
How many speeding tickets
have you got?

551
00:27:50,467 --> 00:27:52,800
-怕是扣了9分了。
-扣了9分。
-Nine points, I'm afraid.
-Nine points.

552
00:27:54,033 --> 00:27:55,567
那你太太被扣了多少分？
How many points
has your wife got?

553
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:56,900
一分没扣。
None.

554
00:27:56,933 --> 00:27:58,167
怎么，你没把分全甩给她驾照去顶？
Well, you've not shovelled
them onto her licence?

555
00:27:58,200 --> 00:27:59,367
这倒真没有。
I haven't.

556
00:27:59,367 --> 00:28:01,433
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

557
00:28:01,467 --> 00:28:03,700
“不好意思啊亲爱的，
你又超速被抓了。”
"Sorry, darling,
you've been caught
speeding again."

558
00:28:05,733 --> 00:28:07,033
我提过这茬，但是……
I suggested it, but...

559
00:28:07,067 --> 00:28:08,133
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGH)

560
00:28:08,167 --> 00:28:10,033
好吧。那你平时开什么车？
Right. And you drive?

561
00:28:10,067 --> 00:28:11,633
一辆阿尔法·罗密欧 156。
An Alfa Romeo 156.

562
00:28:11,667 --> 00:28:15,400
看到没？
这哥们儿开的是阿尔法，
而且开得飞快！
You see?
The man drives an Alfa
and he drives it fast!

563
00:28:15,433 --> 00:28:19,633
当你告诉内阁成员
你要来我们节目时，
他们怎么说？
What did the Cabinet say
when you told them
you were coming here?

564
00:28:19,667 --> 00:28:21,600
他们其实还不知道。
阿利斯泰尔知道。
They don't actually know.
Alistair knows.

565
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:23,767
瞧吧，他们马上就知道了……
You see, they will know...

566
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:25,733
剩下的内阁大臣们现在肯定都
吓得缩在沙发后面，
The rest of them will be
behind their sofas now

567
00:28:25,767 --> 00:28:27,600
死死捂着耳朵
不敢听呢。
with their hands
over their ears.

568
00:28:27,633 --> 00:28:29,200
行，那咱们先从
一个简单的问题开始。
Okay, so let's start
with a simple one.

569
00:28:29,233 --> 00:28:31,600
时速70英里时的刹车距离
是多少？
What's the stopping distance
from 70mph?

570
00:28:31,633 --> 00:28:33,000
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

571
00:28:33,033 --> 00:28:34,467
（笑声）
(LAUGHING)

572
00:28:35,233 --> 00:28:36,533
我能场外连线求助朋友吗？
Can I phone a friend?

573
00:28:36,567 --> 00:28:40,167
不行。你只能靠自己。
求助锦囊已经全用光了。
No. You're on your own.
Used all your lifelines.

574
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:42,500
《公路法规》上写的是
315英尺。
Highway Code says
it's 315 feet.

575
00:28:42,533 --> 00:28:44,000
我相信《公路法规》是没错的。
I'm sure the Highway code
is right.

576
00:28:44,033 --> 00:28:45,500
大错特错。
It's wrong.

577
00:28:45,533 --> 00:28:47,667
-阿斯顿·马丁
一半距离就能刹停。
-对。
-An Aston Martin
will pull up in half that.
-Right.

578
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:50,233
那凭什么阿斯顿·马丁
不能开两倍限速？
So why can't Astons
go twice the speed limit?

579
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:54,533
-这想法挺清奇。
-（轻笑）
-It's a thought.
-(CHUCKLES)

580
00:28:55,067 --> 00:28:56,400
倒是个思路。
It's a thought.

581
00:28:58,500 --> 00:29:00,767
但司机的反应距离可不会变，
Thinking distance
won't be any different there

582
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:02,533
毕竟方向盘后面
坐的还是普通人。
when they're driven by
the same people.

583
00:29:02,567 --> 00:29:04,433
开阿斯顿·马丁的人反应可灵了！
Aston Martin drivers
are sharp!

584
00:29:04,467 --> 00:29:06,067
他们机敏得很，
大多是足球明星，
They're on it,
they're mostly footballers,

585
00:29:06,100 --> 00:29:07,833
砰的一下，
说刹就刹住了，就这么干脆。
and bang,
they're there, like that.

586
00:29:07,867 --> 00:29:10,467
上周来的那个足球运动员
好像撞烂了我们一两辆车吧。
Footballer on last week
seems to have wrecked
one or two of them.

587
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:12,367
没错，他全说中了，
把我们手头的车全撞了个遍。
Yes, he's right.,
every single car we've got.

588
00:29:12,367 --> 00:29:15,267
好了，我实在憋不住了。
And I can sustain this
no longer.

589
00:29:16,233 --> 00:29:17,833
测速摄像头。
Speed cameras.

590
00:29:17,867 --> 00:29:20,367
我们必须得聊聊测速摄像头。
We need to talk speed cameras.

591
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:23,133
你能向我证明
这玩意儿真能救人命吗？
Could you prove to me
they save lives?

592
00:29:23,167 --> 00:29:27,067
当然。全世界做过的
每一项相关研究
Yes. Every study
that's ever been done
anywhere in the world

593
00:29:27,100 --> 00:29:28,667
都表明它们确实管用。
has shown that they work.

594
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:31,233
扯淡，那算哪门子证据。
纯粹是你在那儿瞎嚷嚷。
No, that's not proof.
That's just you
making a noise.

595
00:29:32,400 --> 00:29:35,400
证明……给我证明它们
哪怕拯救过一条命。
Prove... Prove to me that
they have saved a life.

596
00:29:35,433 --> 00:29:37,567
好吧，根据我们汇总的统计数据，
Well, the statistics
that we've gathered together

597
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:40,933
在“安全合作组织”推行的
前三年里，
over the first three years
of the Safety Partnership

598
00:29:40,967 --> 00:29:44,533
数据显示光是在英国本土
就挽救了数百条生命。
show that they're saving
hundreds of lives
in this country alone.

599
00:29:44,567 --> 00:29:46,167
但你八成也看过那些数据吧，
But you've looked at
the figures presumably,

600
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:48,500
比如刚推行限速法规那会儿的数据，
from say when the speed limit
was introduced,

601
00:29:48,533 --> 00:29:51,200
高速公路上的事故，
比如从1965年左右算起。
the motorway ones,
say around '65.

602
00:29:51,233 --> 00:29:54,367
事故率一直逐年下降，
直到1992年，对吧？
It fell every single year
until '92?

603
00:29:54,367 --> 00:29:55,400
没错。
Yeah.

604
00:29:55,433 --> 00:29:56,700
等测速摄像头一装，
When speed cameras
were introduced,

605
00:29:56,733 --> 00:29:57,933
下降趋势就彻底走平了。
then it levelled out.

606
00:29:57,967 --> 00:30:00,567
但我们已经做了
三项专项研究，
But we've also done
three studies already

607
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:02,967
目前正在等待
第四项研究的结果，
and we're just waiting for
the results of a fourth one

608
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,867
这项研究对比了
which compares
the accident rates

609
00:30:05,900 --> 00:30:08,733
安装了摄像头的路段
on the sites where
the cameras are now placed

610
00:30:08,767 --> 00:30:10,100
在安装前后的事故率。
before and after cameras.

611
00:30:10,133 --> 00:30:11,533
所以我们知道它们是管用的。
So we know they're working.

612
00:30:11,567 --> 00:30:14,533
本来只有一起事故，
突然增加到了四起，
If you have one accident,
It suddenly goes up to four

613
00:30:14,567 --> 00:30:15,833
于是你们就在那儿装了个测速摄像头。
and you put
a speed camera there.

614
00:30:15,867 --> 00:30:17,733
事故又回落到了一起……
It goes back to one...

615
00:30:17,767 --> 00:30:20,833
每个特定路段必须发生过四起事故，
才能批准安装测速摄像头。
There has to be four
at every particular site
before you get a speed camera.

616
00:30:20,867 --> 00:30:22,933
-行，那就拿M4公路当个绝佳例子。
-好的。
-Okay, let's take the M4
as a prime example.
-Yes.

617
00:30:22,967 --> 00:30:25,367
-你知道那四起事故里有一桩是什么吗？
-我不知道。
-Do you know
what one of the four was?
-I don't.

618
00:30:25,367 --> 00:30:27,100
有人从桥上跳下去了。
Somebody jumped off
a bridge.

619
00:30:27,133 --> 00:30:28,400
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

620
00:30:28,433 --> 00:30:30,367
我没开玩笑。
其中一桩真就是这个。
I'm not joking.
That was what one of them was.

621
00:30:30,367 --> 00:30:32,100
警方都说了只有一起事故
是因为超速引起的，
The police said only
one of them was
down to speed,

622
00:30:32,133 --> 00:30:33,533
结果你们还是在那儿装了测速摄像头。
and yet they put
speed cameras there.

623
00:30:33,567 --> 00:30:36,967
除了必须有四个人卷入
As well as having four people
involved in injuries

624
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:39,233
导致死亡或重伤的交通事故外，
which either killed them
or seriously injured them.

625
00:30:39,267 --> 00:30:43,233
还必须有证据表明
该路段存在系统性的超速行为。
But also has to be
systematic evidence
of speeding at those sites.

626
00:30:43,267 --> 00:30:47,133
那为什么诺森比亚和达勒姆的
警察局长都会公开表示，
So why do you
have chief constables
in Northumbria and Durham

627
00:30:47,167 --> 00:30:49,267
测速摄像头根本救不了人命？
saying that speed cameras
don't save lives?

628
00:30:49,367 --> 00:30:50,600
呃，他们可不是这么说的。
Well, that's
not what they say.

629
00:30:50,633 --> 00:30:53,100
他们认为在各自管辖的地区，
They believe that they
can achieve in their areas

630
00:30:53,133 --> 00:30:54,700
可以通过其他手段达到同样的效果。
similar results
by other means.

631
00:30:54,733 --> 00:30:56,900
而且我们一直向他们强调的一点，
And one of the things
we've been saying to them

632
00:30:56,933 --> 00:31:00,467
同时也是政策规定的一部分，就是他们必须排查并否定
and part of the policy
is that they have
to have ruled out

633
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:04,200
所有能让该路段更安全的其他途径，
every other opportunity
to make that site safer

634
00:31:04,233 --> 00:31:06,000
之后才能在那里安装摄像头。
before they can put
a camera there.

635
00:31:06,033 --> 00:31:07,733
行，那咱们退一步按这个逻辑来推，
Okay, well, let's work
on this basis then

636
00:31:07,767 --> 00:31:12,800
现在公路上跑着多少，
两千八百万辆机动车，
if you've got what,
28 million cars,
vehicles on the road now,

637
00:31:12,833 --> 00:31:15,533
难道你就不承认，其中一部分车
don't you accept
it is inevitable
that some of them

638
00:31:15,567 --> 00:31:17,633
偶尔撞在一起是不可避免的吗？
occasionally are going
to crash into each other?

639
00:31:17,667 --> 00:31:19,567
完全承认。这点毫无疑问。
Absolutely. There's no
question about that.

640
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:22,400
-而且现在每年死亡人数是3500人。
-是的。
-And we're at 3,500
deaths a year now.
-Yeah.

641
00:31:22,433 --> 00:31:26,300
差不多有……怎么说，
十年了吧。
And have been, give or take,
for what, ten years.

642
00:31:26,333 --> 00:31:28,733
过去这几年，
这数字可一直在稳步下降。
It's been coming down steadily
over the last few years.

643
00:31:28,767 --> 00:31:30,967
大概在3200
到3500之间。
It's around between 3,200
and 3,500.

644
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,100
目前差不多
是3200。
It's about 3,200
at the moment.

645
00:31:33,133 --> 00:31:35,667
你看，但这数字基本都在同一个水平徘徊。
Now, but it's been hovering
around the same mark.

646
00:31:35,700 --> 00:31:37,300
我们大可以拿差个十来个
在这做文章……
We can juggle around
with the odd ten...

647
00:31:37,333 --> 00:31:38,700
它才没有在同一个水平徘徊……
It hasn't been hovering
around the same mark...

648
00:31:38,733 --> 00:31:41,867
你的统计数据到底是谁做的？
根本就不是这么回事。
Who does
your statistics for you?
That's just not true.

649
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:44,000
-要我把数据念给你听吗？
-有本事你就念。
-So, I give you the figures?
-You can give me the figures.

650
00:31:44,033 --> 00:31:47,400
92年，降到了3800。
'92, we got down to 3,800.

651
00:31:47,433 --> 00:31:50,700
3600、3600、3500、
3500、3400、3400……
3,600, 3,600, 3,500,
3,500, 3,400, 3,400

652
00:31:50,733 --> 00:31:54,533
-3400、3400、3400、
3500、3200。
-对啊。
-3,400, 3,400, 3,400,
3,500, 3,200.
-Yeah.

653
00:31:54,567 --> 00:31:55,800
所以我才说……
So I'm saying...

654
00:31:55,833 --> 00:31:58,633
这十年里就只有一年上升过。
It's gone up once in 10 years
for one year.

655
00:31:58,667 --> 00:32:00,333
在那前一年也上升了。
It went up the year
before that, as well.

656
00:32:00,367 --> 00:32:02,100
再前一年也是。
And the year before that.

657
00:32:02,133 --> 00:32:04,367
可你刚才念的那整段时期，
明明整体都在往下降。
But that whole period
that you read out,
it's on the way down.

658
00:32:04,367 --> 00:32:05,567
-才没有！
-就是有！
-It isn't!
-It is!

659
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:07,133
你自己刚刚才念完的数据！
You just read out the figures!

660
00:32:07,167 --> 00:32:09,500
行吧，
那我给你说具体点。
All right,
I'll be more specific.

661
00:32:09,533 --> 00:32:11,800
3421……
3,421...

662
00:32:11,833 --> 00:32:13,100
这还是装了测速摄像头之后。
This is with speed cameras.

663
00:32:13,133 --> 00:32:15,133
下一年是3423。
The next year is 3,423.

664
00:32:15,167 --> 00:32:16,700
这可是暴涨了整整两个……
That's a jump of two...

665
00:32:16,733 --> 00:32:19,400
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

666
00:32:19,433 --> 00:32:23,833
再下一年，降了17个，
然后又暴涨了40个……
In the following year,
it went down by 17,
then it went up by 40...

667
00:32:23,867 --> 00:32:25,733
反正我相信你平时肯定遵守限速，
I'm sure you obey
the speed limit, anyway,

668
00:32:25,767 --> 00:32:28,200
那你到底为什么反对测速摄像头？
so what's your objection
to speed cameras?

669
00:32:28,233 --> 00:32:29,833
我为什么反对测速摄像头？
My objection to speed cameras?

670
00:32:29,867 --> 00:32:32,433
我们把它涂成显眼的黄色，
装在你能看得一清二楚的地方，
We paint them yellow,
we put them
where you can see them,

671
00:32:32,467 --> 00:32:34,500
我们立了个大牌子提醒你
前方有测速，
we put a big sign up
to tell you where
they come in

672
00:32:34,533 --> 00:32:36,367
甚至还在网上公布了测速点清单。
and we even print a list
of them on the internet.

673
00:32:36,367 --> 00:32:38,700
要是这样你还能被拍，
那能怪谁呢？
if you're still
getting caught,
who's fault is that?

674
00:32:39,033 --> 00:32:40,267
噢！
Ooh!

675
00:32:40,367 --> 00:32:41,900
（观众笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

676
00:32:43,367 --> 00:32:44,867
-你这……
-（观众鼓掌）
-You're...
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

677
00:32:47,633 --> 00:32:49,500
被扣了九分的人可是你。
You're the one
with nine points.

678
00:32:49,533 --> 00:32:51,433
-呃，我那是……
-我可是一分都没被扣。
-Well, I've been...
-I haven't got any.

679
00:32:51,467 --> 00:32:52,600
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLES)

680
00:32:54,733 --> 00:32:56,200
这纯粹是……
It's just...

681
00:32:56,233 --> 00:32:57,633
我对测速摄像头是这么看的。
This is my thing
with speed cameras.

682
00:32:57,667 --> 00:32:58,900
如果你真想让人减速，
If you want somebody
to slow down,

683
00:32:58,933 --> 00:33:02,033
打个比方，老生常谈了，
在学校门口，对吧？
say, it's a cliche,
outside a school, okay?

684
00:33:02,067 --> 00:33:03,833
你在学校门口装一个，
You put it outside a school,

685
00:33:03,867 --> 00:33:06,133
漆成粉红色，画上大黄花，
搞成超显眼的霓虹灯测速探头。
you paint it pink,
give it big yellow flowers,
big neon speed camera.

686
00:33:06,167 --> 00:33:07,467
保准没人敢超速开过去。
Nobody will speed past it.

687
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:10,367
这样你就能在物理层面上
彻底制止超速。
You will therefore
physically stop speeding.

688
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:11,967
这是好事啊。
不正是你们想要的吗？
That's a good thing.
Isn't that what you want?

689
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:13,433
是啊，我们不就是这么做的吗？
Yes, and that's what we do?

690
00:33:13,467 --> 00:33:17,233
那你刚才为什么否决了
再增加500台测速摄像头的提议？
So, why have you just said no
to 500 more speed cameras.

691
00:33:17,267 --> 00:33:19,767
因为我认为，
我们必须要做的一件事，
Because, I think
one of the things
we got to do

692
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:21,667
就是重新赢回广大车主
对摄像头的信任。
is win back motorist's
confidence in them.

693
00:33:21,700 --> 00:33:26,500
你刚才表达的，
正是外面许多车主的心声。
You're displaying,
you know, the sentiments
of many motorists out there.

694
00:33:26,533 --> 00:33:30,233
而我觉得，
等我们发布了四年期评估报告，
Now, I think that
when we produce
the four-year report,

695
00:33:30,267 --> 00:33:32,067
我们就能跟车主达成共识，
we can strike a deal
with the motorist

696
00:33:32,100 --> 00:33:35,200
向大家证明，
我们并不是冲着你们的钱包来的，
where we can demonstrate
that we're not after
your money,

697
00:33:35,233 --> 00:33:38,867
我们只是想让危险路段
变得更安全。
we're just trying to make
dangerous places safer.

698
00:33:38,900 --> 00:33:42,367
作为回报，
车主们也会更加自觉遵守限速。
And in return,
the motorist will respect
the speed limits better.

699
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:44,567
我可一秒都没怀疑过你们是冲着钱来的。
I don't think for a moment
you're after our money.

700
