00:45:31,133 --> 00:45:33,700
我们根本出不去了，对吧？
We're not going to
get out there, are we?

968
00:45:33,733 --> 00:45:38,467
不仅车卡在出口大门，
我也被困在车里，
Not only was the car
stuck in the doorway,
but I was stuck in the car,

969
00:45:38,500 --> 00:45:41,067
连车门都推不开。
unable to open the door.

970
00:45:41,100 --> 00:45:43,900
这下场面
真有点尴尬了。
This is slightly
embarrassing now.

971
00:45:43,933 --> 00:45:46,900
一堆人在那儿围观。
A lot of people looking.

972
00:45:46,933 --> 00:45:51,067
哈蒙德：与此同时，杰里米
已经笑得没力气
过来帮忙了。
HAMMOND: Jeremy, meanwhile,
was finding it hard
to come and help.

973
00:45:51,100 --> 00:45:52,567
真是体面极了。
That's dignified.

974
00:45:52,600 --> 00:45:55,567
而詹姆斯
压根懒得管。
And James
couldn't be bothered.

975
00:45:55,600 --> 00:45:59,233
至少我们没引人围观，
要是那样可就太尴尬了。
At least we're not making
a spectacle.
That would be embarrassing.

976
00:45:59,267 --> 00:46:00,833
（喇叭声此起彼伏）
(HORNS TOOTING)

977
00:46:00,867 --> 00:46:02,433
前面堵什么呢？
What's the problem?

978
00:46:04,067 --> 00:46:05,367
我的天呐！
Jesus!

979
00:46:09,067 --> 00:46:12,633
如果你正琢磨着
买辆超跑，
我的建议是：
If you're thinking
about buying a supercar,
my suggestion is,

980
00:46:12,667 --> 00:46:15,500
买归买，但千万别
开进任何繁华市区。
yes, just don't go
near a built-up area with it.

981
00:46:15,533 --> 00:46:17,867
巴黎！超跑！
光鲜浪漫！
Paris! Supercars!
Glamour!

982
00:46:18,433 --> 00:46:19,800
呵，可不是嘛。
Yeah.

983
00:46:19,833 --> 00:46:21,533
（喇叭狂响）
(HORNS HONKING)

984
00:46:24,367 --> 00:46:27,133
老实讲，把他那辆车弄出来
纯属白费劲，
Getting his car out of here
is academic, frankly,

985
00:46:27,167 --> 00:46:30,700
因为那辆福特比风之子还宽，
我觉得根本钻不过……
because I don't think the
Ford, which is wider than that
is gonna fit through...

986
00:46:30,733 --> 00:46:32,700
钻不过这里。
Fit through here.

987
00:46:32,733 --> 00:46:36,500
克拉克森：这对堵在我们后面的车主来说，
可真是个“令人欣慰”的好消息。
CLARKSON: This was
reassuring news for
the people stuck behind us.

988
00:46:39,200 --> 00:46:41,267
我们真把这辆Zonda给拆了。
We've actually
dismantled the Zonda.

989
00:46:41,367 --> 00:46:44,400
把前扰流板上的
这块给卸了下来。
Taken this off
its front spoiler.

990
00:46:45,233 --> 00:46:46,867
就是现在！
This is it!

991
00:46:46,900 --> 00:46:49,467
这绝对是我这辈子开过
最刺激的一段路！
The most exciting
piece of driving
I have ever done!

992
00:46:49,500 --> 00:46:52,100
大家伙儿都在盯着呢，
不过你可别受影响。
Everybody's watching,
but don't let that
put you off.

993
00:46:52,133 --> 00:46:53,733
克拉克森：完全没人围观嘛。
CLARKSON: No crowd here at all

994
00:46:53,767 --> 00:46:55,200
（大笑）
(LAUGHING)

995
00:46:55,233 --> 00:46:57,033
好嘞，我上了。
Right, here I go.

996
00:46:57,067 --> 00:47:00,267
克拉克森：我觉得等会儿
咱们又得捡几块Zonda的零件了。
CLARKSON: I think
we might be picking up
some more bits of Zonda.

997
00:47:02,200 --> 00:47:04,000
-（咔嚓刮蹭声）
-哎哟！
-(CRUNCHING)
-Ooh!

998
00:47:04,033 --> 00:47:05,733
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGHING)

999
00:47:07,633 --> 00:47:09,467
哎哟！听着就贵！
Ooh! Sounded expensive.

1000
00:47:11,433 --> 00:47:13,267
克拉克森：我简直没眼看了。
CLARKSON: I can't watch this.

1001
00:47:13,967 --> 00:47:15,367
我真是太爱车了。
I like cars too much.

1002
00:47:18,167 --> 00:47:19,667
（笑声）我出来了！
(LAUGHING) I'm out!

1003
00:47:20,600 --> 00:47:22,800
-漂亮！他钻过来了！
-（鼓掌）
-Yes! He's through!
-(APPLAUDS)

1004
00:47:23,367 --> 00:47:24,433
太棒了！
Bravo!

1005
00:47:27,267 --> 00:47:30,133
克拉克森：接下来
轮到这个
宽体大块头了。
CLARKSON: And then
it was the turn
of the wide boy.

1006
00:47:36,367 --> 00:47:38,900
哈蒙德：天哪，这简直
窄得令人发指！
HAMMOND: Oh, man, that is
unbelievably tight!

1007
00:47:39,667 --> 00:47:41,400
（喇叭齐鸣）
(HORNS TOOTING)

1008
00:47:41,433 --> 00:47:43,533
你那边蹭着没？
You all right on that side?

1009
00:47:51,367 --> 00:47:52,867
简直是在贴着蹭……
That is brushing...

1010
00:47:52,900 --> 00:47:54,133
噢，没错。
Oh, yes.

1011
00:47:58,400 --> 00:48:00,567
我们算是把整个巴黎给搞瘫痪了！
We've sort of stopped Paris!

1012
00:48:00,600 --> 00:48:02,967
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGHING)

1013
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:05,867
詹姆斯：我二十秒之内
就能搞定开出来。
MAY: I'll be out of here
in less than 20 seconds.

1014
00:48:06,867 --> 00:48:08,200
克拉克森：慢点！
CLARKSON: Slowly!

1015
00:48:08,233 --> 00:48:10,367
（喇叭齐鸣）
(HORNS TOOTING)

1016
00:48:10,367 --> 00:48:12,367
克拉克森：来，走着。
哈蒙德：一点一点挪。
CLARKSON: Come on.
HAMMOND: Inch it.

1017
00:48:15,633 --> 00:48:16,933
妥了，你出来了。
Yup. You're out.

1018
00:48:16,967 --> 00:48:18,467
大功告成。
That's it.

1019
00:48:19,900 --> 00:48:21,567
堵成长龙了，没错。
There's a jam. Yes.

1020
00:48:21,600 --> 00:48:24,800
所有这帮人都被咱们
堵在这儿干等着。
All these people have been
kept waiting by us.

1021
00:48:24,833 --> 00:48:26,167
而且他们看着都气炸了。
And they look cross.

1022
00:48:27,833 --> 00:48:29,233
管他呢！
Still!

1023
00:48:30,067 --> 00:48:31,567
（轻笑）
(CHUCKLING)

1024
00:48:41,400 --> 00:48:45,367
好了，出发。
五百英里，全程狂飙。
Right, here we go.
500 miles, all of them fast.

1025
00:48:49,967 --> 00:48:51,700
克拉克森：重回大路之后，
CLARKSON: Back on the road,

1026
00:48:51,733 --> 00:48:54,900
我们又进入了日常保留节目——
互喷对方的车。
we got into the routine
of finding fault,
with each other's cars.

1027
00:48:57,233 --> 00:48:59,433
那台Zonda……
That Zonda...

1028
00:48:59,467 --> 00:49:02,600
活像一只
套着橙色工装背带裤的狮子……
It's like a lion
in orange dungarees...

1029
00:49:02,633 --> 00:49:06,600
既威风凛凛，
又滑稽至极。
Kind of fierce
but ridiculous,
all at the same time.

1030
00:49:06,633 --> 00:49:08,767
哈蒙德：这台法拉利的问题在于，
HAMMOND: The problem
with the Ferrari is,

1031
00:49:08,800 --> 00:49:11,200
它还是显得稍微
低调沉闷了点，
it is that little bit
more understated,

1032
00:49:11,233 --> 00:49:13,400
超跑可不能这么低调。
and that's no good
in a supercar.

1033
00:49:13,433 --> 00:49:15,367
超跑就该极尽浮夸、嚣张跋扈。
It's supposed to be loud
and over the top.

1034
00:49:15,367 --> 00:49:18,033
去参加变装派对，
你就该扮成一根大胡萝卜。
Go to a fancy dress party
you're supposed to come
as a carrot.

1035
00:49:18,067 --> 00:49:19,533
或者一只硕大的耗子！
Or a big mouse!

1036
00:49:22,633 --> 00:49:26,500
杰里米上来了。
听听这令人魂牵梦绕的五金铺破铜烂铁声。
Here comes Jeremy.
Listen to the evocative sound
of ironmongery.

1037
00:49:30,800 --> 00:49:33,633
挺有意思的是，我觉得
Zonda这种车
Interestingly, I think
Zonda is the sort of car

1038
00:49:33,667 --> 00:49:36,233
纯粹是给那些过度操心
自己牙齿的人开的。
for people who worry too much
about their teeth.

1039
00:49:36,267 --> 00:49:38,900
哈蒙德：
我根本没去漂白过牙齿！
HAMMOND:
I have not had my teeth done!

1040
00:49:43,033 --> 00:49:45,467
杰里米已经连轴狂奔了
Jeremy's been on the go for

1041
00:49:45,500 --> 00:49:48,133
居然有五到十分钟
没去加油了。
five or 10 minutes now
without re-fuelling.

1042
00:49:48,167 --> 00:49:50,167
脚底下油门踩得
肯定贼温柔。
Must have been very light
on the throttle.

1043
00:49:55,400 --> 00:49:57,500
哈蒙德：加完油后，
天开始下起雨来，
HAMMOND: After the fill-up,
it started to rain,

1044
00:49:57,533 --> 00:50:00,600
对我们绝大多数人来说，
这根本就不是事儿。
which wasn't a problem
at all, for most of us.

1045
00:50:00,867 --> 00:50:02,367
别啊，千万别！
No, no!

1046
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:04,433
我得找个路口下高速！
I need a junction!

1047
00:50:04,833 --> 00:50:06,367
（笑）
(LAUGHS)

1048
00:50:06,900 --> 00:50:08,133
求你了！
Please!

1049
00:50:12,967 --> 00:50:16,567
克拉克森：
随着里程不断累积，
有一点变得显而易见。
CLARKSON:
As the miles racked up,
one thing became clear.

1050
00:50:16,600 --> 00:50:19,900
这台福特绝对是
最舒服、最文明的。
The Ford was easily
the most civilised.

1051
00:50:21,733 --> 00:50:24,600
掐指一算，
理查德的屁股
现在估计已经被颠烂了。
Round about now,
Richard's buttocks
are going to be ruined.

1052
00:50:26,967 --> 00:50:28,400
屁股彻底麻了。
Numb bum.

1053
00:50:29,367 --> 00:50:31,800
而我这儿依然爽得不行。
And I'm so comfortable still.

1054
00:50:36,533 --> 00:50:39,067
梅：好了，
按我的计算，
MAY: Right,
by my calculations,

1055
00:50:39,100 --> 00:50:41,633
大概还剩150英里，
about 150 miles to go

1056
00:50:41,667 --> 00:50:46,200
我觉得是时候
给这趟行程
整点儿乐子了。
and I think it's time
we made things
a bit more interesting.

1057
00:50:46,233 --> 00:50:48,733
克拉克森：啥意思，
你是在建议
我们下高速？
CLARKSON: What,
you're suggesting
we turn off the motorway?

1058
00:50:48,767 --> 00:50:51,700
梅：不是建议，
我们必须下高速。
MAY: Not suggesting,
but we are turning off
the motorway.

1059
00:50:51,733 --> 00:50:53,900
天呐，杰里米，
这听着可不妙。
Oh, crikey, Jeremy,
that sounds bad.

1060
00:50:55,267 --> 00:50:57,367
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINES ROARING)

1061
00:51:19,400 --> 00:51:24,200
梅：在高速公路上，
福特和风之子的蛮力
确实难逢敌手。
MAY: On the motorway,
the brute force of the Ford
and Zonda was hard to match.

1062
00:51:24,233 --> 00:51:28,333
现在是时候在乡间小路上
看看谁才是真正的大哥了。
Now it was time to see
who was the boss
on the back roads.

1063
00:51:29,300 --> 00:51:31,567
不过在那之前，不可避免地……
But, first, inevitably...

1064
00:51:39,033 --> 00:51:41,133
他怎么又要加？！
How can he need more?

1065
00:51:41,167 --> 00:51:43,067
你注意到没有，
他的右手二头肌
Have you noticed
how his right bicep

1066
00:51:43,100 --> 00:51:44,867
现在已经比左手大了一圈？
is now slightly bigger
than his left one?

1067
00:51:44,900 --> 00:51:46,800
（哈蒙德大笑）
(HAMMOND LAUGHS)

1068
00:51:46,833 --> 00:51:49,600
你有没有发现，
他每次给车加油的时候，
站姿都跟个茶壶似的？
Have you also noticed
that when he fills his car up,
he stands like a teapot?

1069
00:51:49,633 --> 00:51:52,000
（哈蒙德笑个不停）
(HAMMOND LAUGHING)

1070
00:51:52,033 --> 00:51:53,433
克拉克森：詹姆斯，
我钱花光了！
CLARKSON: James,
I've run out of money!

1071
00:51:53,467 --> 00:51:54,633
-是吗？
-（哈蒙德大笑）
-Have you?
-(HAMMOND LAUGHS)

1072
00:51:54,667 --> 00:51:55,967
这处境
可真是太有意思了！
What an
interesting predicament!

1073
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:57,400
求你了，能不能借我点钱？
Please can I borrow
some money?

1074
00:51:57,433 --> 00:51:58,700
我们可不会
为了这事儿捞你。
We're not
bailing you for that.

1075
00:51:58,733 --> 00:52:00,567
你想让我替你出油钱？
You want me to pay
for your petrol?

1076
00:52:00,600 --> 00:52:02,467
对。
Yes.

1077
00:52:02,500 --> 00:52:05,033
行吧，
全国人民可都看着呢。
Right.
The nation is observing.

1078
00:52:05,067 --> 00:52:06,367
我是真没钱了！
I haven't got any money!

1079
00:52:06,367 --> 00:52:08,500
就由我来资助你这荒唐的汽油瘾吧。
I will fund your ridiculous
petrol habit.

1080
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:15,700
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINE ROARING)

1081
00:52:15,733 --> 00:52:19,433
很好，这下法拉利
该把面子找回来了。
Right, this is where
the Ferrari claws it back.

1082
00:52:22,833 --> 00:52:26,467
你看，那两位脚底下踩的
是大号的、
See, what the other two
have there are great big,

1083
00:52:26,500 --> 00:52:29,667
粗笨厚重的
工人劳保靴。
coarse, heavy,
workman's boots.

1084
00:52:30,733 --> 00:52:34,700
而我这台车
犹如芭蕾舞演员的足尖鞋。
What I have here
is a ballerina's point shoe.

1085
00:52:36,133 --> 00:52:38,867
突然间，这台Zonda
感觉好宽啊！噢！
Suddenly, the Zonda
feels quite wide! Ooh!

1086
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:43,000
我这车有碳陶刹车盘，
I've got ceramic discs,

1087
00:52:43,033 --> 00:52:45,033
还有个叫E-diff的电子差速器，
I've got something
called an E-diff,

1088
00:52:45,067 --> 00:52:48,267
迈克尔·舒马赫的F1赛车上
也有同款。
which Michael Schumacher
also has on his F1 car.

1089
00:52:48,367 --> 00:52:52,633
我还有个五档调节的
牵引力控制旋钮。
I've got a five-position
traction control centre.

1090
00:52:59,600 --> 00:53:03,500
说老实话，
在这条路上我真想开那辆法拉利，
To be honest,
I'd love to be driving
that Ferrari on this road

1091
00:53:03,533 --> 00:53:07,633
因为那台车
简直是机械工程学上的杰作。
'cos it is a piece
of engineering brilliance,
that car.

1092
00:53:09,667 --> 00:53:12,100
但我绝不想开
理查德那辆。
I wouldn't like to be driving
Richard's car.

1093
00:53:13,967 --> 00:53:15,500
（胎响尖叫）
(TYRES SQUEAL)

1094
00:53:16,133 --> 00:53:17,533
我刚才一点都没慌。
I wasn't worried.

1095
00:53:18,700 --> 00:53:21,400
你不是该配有
牵引力控制系统吗！
You're supposed
to have traction control!

1096
00:53:22,433 --> 00:53:23,533
（笑声）
(LAUGHS)

1097
00:53:27,400 --> 00:53:29,100
“龟速船长”追上来啦！
Here comes Captain Slow!

1098
00:53:30,600 --> 00:53:32,600
这玩意儿简直太神奇了！
It's absolute magic,
this thing!

1099
00:53:34,100 --> 00:53:37,533
克拉克森：虽说有时候，
詹姆斯的认路水平确实掉链子，
CLARKSON: Sometimes,
James's sense of direction
let him down a bit

1100
00:53:37,567 --> 00:53:41,700
但毫无疑问，在这种路况下，
他的车确实神了，
but there was no doubt
that in this terrain
his car was brilliant,

1101
00:53:41,733 --> 00:53:45,067
我也以一贯优雅大度的风度
承认了这一点。
a point I conceded
with typical good grace.

1102
00:53:45,100 --> 00:53:47,533
如果你住在法国西南部的峡谷里，
If you live in a gorge
in south west France

1103
00:53:47,567 --> 00:53:50,733
选他那台法拉利绝对舒坦得多。
you're definitely better off
with his Ferrari.

1104
00:53:50,767 --> 00:53:52,433
真的。
You really are.

1105
00:53:55,667 --> 00:53:58,667
哈蒙德：当然了，现实世界里
总有些麻烦，
HAMMOND: Of course,
there are some elements
of the real world

1106
00:53:58,700 --> 00:54:02,633
是连超级跑车都救不了你的。
that even a supercar
can't get you out of.

1107
00:54:07,767 --> 00:54:10,433
克拉克森：我以前可从没见过
你开这么快。
CLARKSON: I've never seen you
drive fast before.

1108
00:54:12,200 --> 00:54:15,433
梅：问题就在这儿，
开快车得讲究特定时机和场合。
MAY: The thing is,
driving fast is for
a particular time and place.

1109
00:54:15,467 --> 00:54:18,700
我能开快，只是偶尔才开，
因为我是个绅士。
I can do it, I just only
do it occasionally,
because I'm a gentleman.

1110
00:54:18,733 --> 00:54:21,633
我可不指望你们俩能懂这个！
I don't expect you two
to understand this!

1111
00:54:21,667 --> 00:54:23,900
你开Zonda真的那么费劲吗？
Are you really struggling
in the Zonda?

1112
00:54:23,933 --> 00:54:25,267
怎么说呢，这台车吧……
Well, the thing about it...

1113
00:54:25,367 --> 00:54:28,233
正常速度开的时候它好开得惊人，
It's amazingly easy to drive
at ordinary speeds,

1114
00:54:28,267 --> 00:54:30,700
尽管长了一副凶悍样，可一旦你深踩油门……
despite looking like it does,
but when you press on...

1115
00:54:30,733 --> 00:54:33,567
就好像你在跟他打自由搏击，过招还挺过瘾。
It's like you tag fight him,
you kick box him,
and it's quite nice.

1116
00:54:33,600 --> 00:54:35,267
接着你说：
“来啊，拿出你的看家本领。”
And then you say,
"Go on then.
Give me your best shot."

1117
00:54:35,367 --> 00:54:36,967
然后他直接把你的脑袋
给拧下来了！
And then he takes
your head off!

1118
00:54:37,000 --> 00:54:39,533
不过我敢说，这辆福特
八成是这里操控最烂的……
But I bet this Ford
is probably the worst
handling car here...

1119
00:54:39,567 --> 00:54:40,667
这点我承认。
I'll concede that.

1120
00:54:40,700 --> 00:54:43,233
设计那副底盘的美国佬
根本就……
No American who designed
that chassis

1121
00:54:43,267 --> 00:54:46,433
压根就不知道
世上居然还有这么一条路。
is even half aware
that a road like this exists.

1122
00:54:46,467 --> 00:54:48,000
嗯，确实很有可能。
Yeah, that would
make sense.

1123
00:54:48,033 --> 00:54:50,667
要是带个美国人来这儿，
他非得当场吓死不可。
If you brought
an American here,
he would die of shock.

1124
00:54:50,700 --> 00:54:53,367
我还能再说一句吗，
要是我们开跑前
Can I just say also,
that if I'd had a look
down there

1125
00:54:53,367 --> 00:54:55,367
我往悬崖下面看了一眼，
before we did this,

1126
00:54:55,367 --> 00:54:57,833
我肯定会退出运动模式，
继续当我的“龟速船长”。
I'd have taken it out of sport
and been Captain Slow again.

1127
00:54:57,867 --> 00:54:59,400
-（笑）
-我是说，你瞧瞧那底下！
-(LAUGHS)
-I mean, look at that!

1128
00:54:59,433 --> 00:55:00,967
你刚才是在比赛吗？
Have you been
in a race?

1129
00:55:01,000 --> 00:55:02,767
也就比了那么一小会儿，
一点都不好玩。
Only vey briefly.
Didn't like it.

1130
00:55:02,800 --> 00:55:05,767
克拉克森：接着我们聊到了
更重要的问题。
CLARKSON: Then we moved on
to more important matters.

1131
00:55:05,800 --> 00:55:09,967
哈蒙德：我真没去
美白过牙齿！
HAMMOND: I have not
had my teeth done!

1132
00:55:10,000 --> 00:55:13,567
克拉克森：然后，就到了
该重新上路的时候了。
CLARKSON: And then it was time
to get back on the road.

1133
00:55:18,367 --> 00:55:20,233
现在我们快到
旅程的终点了，
We were now near
journey's end

1134
00:55:20,267 --> 00:55:24,100
但那场伴随了我们700英里的
激烈争吵依然没有停歇。
and the argument
that had fuelled us
for 700 miles still raged.

1135
00:55:24,133 --> 00:55:26,600
你完全能明白是为什么。
And you can see why.

1136
00:55:26,633 --> 00:55:29,700
Zonda拥有极具张力的外形
和狂暴的动力。
The Zonda has the drama
and the power.

1137
00:55:31,267 --> 00:55:33,200
法拉利有着绝佳的操控，
The Ferrari has the handling

1138
00:55:33,233 --> 00:55:35,700
以及震撼人心的
引擎声浪。
and an astonishing
soundtrack.

1139
00:55:35,733 --> 00:55:38,433
（引擎轰鸣声）
(ENGINE ROARING)

1140
00:55:38,467 --> 00:55:41,667
至于福特呢？
它是最漂亮的，速度最快，
And the Ford?
Well, it's the prettiest
and the fastest

1141
00:55:41,700 --> 00:55:43,367
而且还是最省油的……
and it has
the best fuel economy...

1142
00:55:43,400 --> 00:55:46,233
噢等等，
这句不对吧？
Oh, no, wait,
that's not right, is it?

1143
00:55:46,267 --> 00:55:49,167
总之，每辆车
都依然难分高下，
Each car, then,
was still putting up a fight

1144
00:55:49,200 --> 00:55:51,967
我们谁也不肯退让半步。
and none of us would budge.

1145
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:56,167
开超跑，就得让我感觉
自己像个十岁的小屁孩。
I need to be made to feel
like I'm 10 in a supercar.

1146
00:55:56,200 --> 00:55:58,367
要是不能让我觉得自己正穿着短裤，
If I don't feel like
I'm sitting in short trousers

1147
00:55:58,367 --> 00:56:00,267
张大着嘴巴，
惊呼“哇塞”。
with my mouth open,
going, "Wow."

1148
00:56:00,367 --> 00:56:02,167
那它就算失败了。
Then it's failed.

1149
00:56:03,533 --> 00:56:06,367
梅：法拉利的独到之处
就在于此……
MAY: The thing about Ferrari
is this...

1150
00:56:06,367 --> 00:56:09,167
你能看出它纯正的血统，
You can see the breeding,

1151
00:56:09,200 --> 00:56:12,133
而且能真切感受到它。
and you can feel it.

1152
00:56:12,167 --> 00:56:15,200
你根本没法用理性
去评判这种车。
You can't rationalise
cars like these.

1153
00:56:15,233 --> 00:56:17,733
买它们靠的不是脑子，
They're not something
you buy with your head,

1154
00:56:17,767 --> 00:56:20,100
而是全凭真心，
因为你深爱着它们。
you buy them with your heart,
because you love them.

1155
00:56:20,133 --> 00:56:22,500
谁又能说得清爱是什么呢？
And who can explain love?

1156
00:56:22,533 --> 00:56:26,267
我只知道，
我爱这台大福特
All I know is,
I love this big Ford

1157
00:56:27,133 --> 00:56:30,500
胜过爱其他任何一台。
more than I love the others.

1158
00:56:30,533 --> 00:56:32,467
克拉克森：谁也说服不了谁倒也没关系，
CLARKSON: And it's okay
that we can't agree

1159
00:56:32,500 --> 00:56:36,000
因为别忘了，
我们一路大老远横跨法国，
because, if you remember,
we didn't come all the way
through France

1160
00:56:36,033 --> 00:56:38,800
可不是为了评出谁是最好的超跑。
to find the best supercar.

1161
00:56:38,833 --> 00:56:41,367
我们大老远跑来，就是为了它。
We came here for that.

1162
00:56:48,200 --> 00:56:50,033
克拉克森：
这就是米约高架桥。
CLARKSON:
This is the Millau Bridge.

1163
00:56:50,067 --> 00:56:53,100
它高逾千尺，
是全世界最高的桥。
At 1,000 feet,
it's the tallest bridge
in the world.

1164
00:56:53,133 --> 00:56:58,100
它高到你直接把金丝雀码头摩天楼
塞进桥面底下都绰绰有余。
It's so tall, you could put
Canary Wharf
underneath the roadway.

1165
00:57:03,700 --> 00:57:07,733
而且它精妙绝伦，
热胀冷缩间，桥身起伏能达到
整整十英尺之多，
It's clever, too,
because it rises and falls
by as much as 10 feet,

1166
00:57:07,767 --> 00:57:10,433
全凭气温与季节的变幻。
depending on the temperature
and the season.

1167
00:57:12,400 --> 00:57:17,233
这真是一项
不可思议的奇迹。
It is a magnificent
achievement.

1168
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:22,767
那么，这跟我们这几台又大、又沉、
喝油如流水、贵得要死的车
到底有什么关系？
So what does it have to do
with our big, heavy, thirsty
and expensive cars?

1169
00:57:24,867 --> 00:57:29,833
那就是一台超级跑车，
正如眼前
这是一座超级大桥。
That is a supercar
in the same way
that that is a super bridge.

1170
00:57:29,867 --> 00:57:33,033
他们本可以把桥修低点，
随便用几根工字钢搭几块烂木板完事，
They could have built it
lower down with some RSJs
and some planks of wood,

1171
00:57:33,067 --> 00:57:34,900
但他们没有。
but they didn't.

1172
00:57:34,933 --> 00:57:38,033
他们造出了惊天动地、
令人叹为观止、震撼绝伦的杰作。
They built something amazing,
something astonishing,
something wonderful.

1173
00:57:38,067 --> 00:57:40,167
他们彻底疯魔了。
They went berserk.

1174
00:57:52,600 --> 00:57:55,233
所以，这座大桥，
就像载着我们一路狂飙到此的跑车一样，
This bridge, then,
like the cars
that brought us here

1175
00:57:55,267 --> 00:57:58,767
正是人类本能的终极体现……
is an example of humans
doing what humans do...

1176
00:57:58,800 --> 00:58:01,433
挑战极限，突破自我。
Pushing boundaries,
pushing ourselves.

1177
00:58:01,467 --> 00:58:04,267
挑选一件看似不可能做到的事，
Taking something
that can't be done

1178
00:58:04,367 --> 00:58:06,367
然后把它变成现实。
and then doing it.

1179
00:58:20,367 --> 00:58:22,367
（引擎咆哮）
(ENGINES ROARING)

1180
00:58:30,200 --> 00:58:32,167
（观众欢呼鼓掌）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

1181
00:58:33,533 --> 00:58:35,267
克拉克森：那天真是爽爆了。
CLARKSON: That was a good day.

1182
00:58:35,367 --> 00:58:38,467
那天太棒了，而那……
That was a good day,
and that...

1183
00:58:38,500 --> 00:58:40,267
正好诠释了超级跑车的意义。
That explains supercars.

1184
00:58:40,367 --> 00:58:43,267
这就是人类为了让我们自己
活得更痛快。
It's mankind making life
better for ourselves.

1185
00:58:43,367 --> 00:58:44,833
我是说，这才是最重要的。
I mean, that's
the important thing.

1186
00:58:44,867 --> 00:58:47,867
山顶洞人可不会嫌火太烫，
就把火给灭了。
Caveman did not
snuff out the fire
'cos it was too hot.

1187
00:58:47,900 --> 00:58:50,067
说得一点没错。人们老是在那吹，
You're absolutely right.
People are always saying,

1188
00:58:50,100 --> 00:58:53,367
“海豚智商可高了。”
高个屁，是吧？
"Dolphins are really
intelligent."
But they're not, are they?

1189
00:58:53,367 --> 00:58:55,367
因为它们连个电子差速锁都造不出来。
'Cos they can't even engineer
an E-diff.

1190
00:58:55,367 --> 00:58:57,100
我跟你们讲，节目的最后，
I tell you what,
before we end,

1191
00:58:57,133 --> 00:58:59,467
我这儿有一段希拉克总统的名言，听好了：
I've got a quote here
from President Chirac, okay?

1192
00:58:59,500 --> 00:59:02,500
这是他当年给大桥剪彩时说的。
This is what he said
when he opened that bridge.

1193
00:59:02,533 --> 00:59:04,600
“法国人民理应
"The French people
are rightly proud

1194
00:59:04,633 --> 00:59:06,467
为在这里铸就的伟业
深感自豪，
"of the feats
accomplished here,

1195
00:59:06,500 --> 00:59:08,967
这伟业象征着法国，一个现代的法国，
"feats which speak for France,
a modern France,

1196
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:11,267
一个锐意进取、辉煌璀璨的法国，
"an enterprising,
successful France,

1197
00:59:11,367 --> 00:59:14,633
一个投资未来的法国。”
"a France which invests
in the future."

1198
00:59:14,667 --> 00:59:17,767
他唯独忘了一点没提——
这桥的总设计师是个英国人！
He forgot to mention
the fact the architect
was British!

1199
00:59:17,800 --> 00:59:19,367
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

1200
00:59:19,367 --> 00:59:21,467
伴随着这枚重磅炸弹，
晚安，我们下周见！
And on that bombshell,
good night.
See you next week.

